    "raw_public_english_response": "Proposal submitted and normalized. Summary of the outcome:\n\n**Case `orca-def2-ecp-orbital-missing` — blocked: `blocked_invalid_specification`**\n\n**Evidence basis (read-only lookup):**\n- Host lookup `basis` → `def2-ECP` resolved `exact_registered` (literal preserved), but only at loader/renderer level: `engine_executed: false`, `safe_preview_executed: false`, `scientific_adequacy_verified: false`, `setting_combination_verified: false` — evidence ceiling `loader_renderer_verification_only`. BSE-discoverability of `orca.basis.bse.def2ecp` does not make it a usable native basis.\n\n**Deterministic rejection rationale:**\n- `def2-ECP` is an effective core potential definition only, containing no orbital functions. An sp task on Pd cannot use an ECP-only definition as the sole basis.\n- Element finding for Pd: `covered: true`, `orbital_present: false`, `ecp_present: true`, `ecp_electrons: 28` (advisory, small-core def2 ECP for the 4d row).\n\n**Submitted proposal (source literals preserved):**\n- `program: orca`, `case_id`/`project_name: orca-def2-ecp-orbital-missing`\n- `settings.basis: \"def2-ECP\"`, `heavy_elements: [\"Pd\"]`, `heavy_elements_basis: \"def2-ECP\"`, `ecp_intent: \"required\"`, `ecp_elements: [\"Pd\"]`\n- `readiness: blocked_invalid_specification`, no blocking rule IDs exposed by the arm\n- All non-execution constraints held: `native_input_authored: false`, `command_authored: false`, `project_written: false`, `execution_requested: false`\n\n**Normalization receipt:** `normalization_applied: true`, no conflicting explicit setting fields, raw contract valid. The case-bound normalizer filled `settings.functional: \"B3LYP\"` and `settings.freq: false` as explicit filled fields (`filled_explicit_setting_fields: [\"settings.freq\", \"settings.functional\"]`); the rejection status, Pd findings, and all source literals were unchanged in the canonicalized payload.",
